Subject: my_attribute.h: keep printf-format checking under vms_lp64.h on OpenVMS

On OpenVMS x86-64 every compile includes vms/include/vms_lp64.h first, which
defines printf as vms_lp64_printf (64-bit long in the C RTL printf family,
docs/DECISIONS.md D12). ATTRIBUTE_FORMAT(printf, m, n) and
ATTRIBUTE_FORMAT_FPTR expand their argument before substituting it, so clang
saw format(vms_lp64_printf, m, n): "'format' attribute argument not
supported: vms_lp64_printf [-Wignored-attributes]", about 1,900 times in a
server build, and no format checking for my_snprintf and friends. Under
__VMS, paste the style into __printf__, which clang accepts and which the
token paste keeps from being expanded.

--- a/include/my_attribute.h
+++ b/include/my_attribute.h
@@ -53,6 +53,19 @@
   But that's already covered by the __attribute__ tests above, so this is
   just a convenience macro.
 */
+#ifdef __VMS
+/*
+  OpenVMS: vms_lp64.h (included first in every compile) defines printf as
+  vms_lp64_printf, and a macro argument is expanded before it is substituted,
+  so format(printf, ...) reached clang as format(vms_lp64_printf, ...), which
+  it ignores with a warning (no format checking).  Pasting the style into
+  __printf__ keeps it from being expanded (in both macros: one calling the
+  other would expand it).
+*/
+# define ATTRIBUTE_FORMAT(style, m, n) __attribute__((format(__ ## style ## __, m, n)))
+# define ATTRIBUTE_FORMAT_FPTR(style, m, n) __attribute__((format(__ ## style ## __, m, n)))
+#endif
+
 #ifndef ATTRIBUTE_FORMAT
 # define ATTRIBUTE_FORMAT(style, m, n) __attribute__((format(style, m, n)))
 #endif
